{
  "about": "Agent office layout (contract 4.6). Units are metres; +y is up; the overhead camera looks from +x/+z, so the north (z min) and west (x min) walls are full height and the south/east walls are low cutaway walls. 'rot' is degrees about +y; a POI with rot 0 faces +z. Plan: data core / charging dock with one docking bay per agent (west, behind glass; 4.5 m deep) | a glass meeting room (north-west: video wall + curved console) | work pods in 2 rows of 5 facing west toward the dock (robots sit and plug in) | training pods + a maintenance bar (north-east) | lobby by the door (east wall): scanner gate, wayfinding totem, hang-out seating, showcase, agent board; a painted concourse runs from the door to the dock | the launch pad on the open floor above the factory | deploy line (south), the agent factory: robots hammer and tinker at steel workbenches, new robots roll out of the fabricator and ride the belt to dispatch. One pale lab floor (raised-access panels) throughout; the factory is marked out in floor paint. Colour means status: robots and their desk / bay lights are green (working, deploying, done), yellow (idle, paused, arriving), orange (waiting for you) or red (error); everything else is a muted palette.",
  "agents": {
    "max": 10,
    "_note": "slots the office seats at once: one work pod (desk_grid) and one docking bay (charge_row) per agent, and every agent state must hold this many (overflow stand-<zone> spots are generated). Sessions beyond this queue in the lobby (state queued: they wait on the lobby's stand-entry spots in queue order)."
  },
